Input: {"question": "Who was Mahmud I's father?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "start": 0, "end": 110, "text": "Mahmud I Mahmud I (, , 2 August 1696 13 December 1754) was the Sultan of the Ottoman Empire from 1730 to 1754."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "start": 111, "end": 220, "text": "He was born at Edirne Palace, the son of Mustafa II (1664–1703); his mother was Saliha Sabkati Valide Sultan."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "start": 221, "end": 275, "text": "Mahmud I was the older brother of Osman III (1754–57)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "start": 276, "end": 437, "text": "On 28 September 1730, Patrona Halil with a small group of fellow Janissaries aroused some of the citizens of Constantinople who opposed the reforms of Ahmet III."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "start": 438, "end": 558, "text": "Sweeping up more soldiers Halil led the riot to the Topkapı Palace and demanded the death of the grand vizer, Nevşehirli"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d01", "start": 0, "end": 646, "text": "Mustafa I 14th generation Osman II Şehzade Mehmed Murad IV Şehzade Bayezid Şehzade Süleyman Şehzade Kasım Ibrahim 15th generation Şehzade Ömer Mehmed IV Suleiman II Ahmed II 16th generation Mustafa II Ahmed III Şehzade Ibrahim 17th generation Mahmud I Osman III Şehzade Hasan Şehzade Süleyman Mustafa III Abdul Hamid I Şehzade Mehmed ( son of Ahmed III ) Şehzade Beyazid Şehzade Numan Şehzade Mahmud 18th generation Selim III Mustafa IV Mahmud II Şehzade Abdullah Selim 19th generation Abdulmejid I Abdulaziz Mustafa Efendi 20th generation Murad V Abdul Hamid II Mehmed V Şehzade Ahmed Kemaleddin Şehzade Mehmed Burhaneddin Şehzade Ahmed Nureddin"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02", "start": 0, "end": 101, "text": "Mahmud I of Great Seljuq Nasir ad-Din Mahmud I was the sultan of the Seljuk Empire from 1092 to 1094."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02", "start": 102, "end": 216, "text": "He succeeded Malik Shah I as Sultan, but he did not gain control of the empire built by Malik Shah and Alp Arslan."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02", "start": 217, "end": 353, "text": "Turkan Khatun, the last wife of Malik Shah, tried to win the throne for her 4 years old son Mahmud, who was proclaimed sultan in Bagdad."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02", "start": 354, "end": 482, "text": "The older son of Malik shah, Barkyaruk was proclaimed too, and the armies of the two pretenders meet in Barudjird, near Hamadan."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02", "start": 483, "end": 531, "text": "The forces of Barkyaruk won and took the capital"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "Malik Shah I and proclaimed sultan at Baghdad by the caliph al-Muqtadi ( r."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03", "start": 76, "end": 89, "text": "1075–1094 ) ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03", "start": 90, "end": 175, "text": "Under his notional reign , the empire built by his father and Alp Arslan fragmented ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03", "start": 176, "end": 312, "text": "After Mahmud 's forces lost a battle at Borujerd , he and his mother were assassinated by the family of the former vizir Nizam al-Mulk ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03", "start": 313, "end": 545, "text": "Mahmud I Gold dinar of Mahmud I , minted at Isfahan in 1093 or 1094 Sultan of the Seljuk Empire Reign 19 November 1092 – October 1094 Coronation 19 November 1092 Predecessor Malik Shah I Successor Berkyaruq Regent Terken Khatun Born"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d04", "start": 0, "end": 290, "text": "1088 Died October 1094 ( 1094-10-00 ) ( aged 5–6 ) Names Nasir al-Din Mahmud I Father Malik Shah I Mother Terken Khatun Religion Sunni Islam Life edit In 1092 , when Malik Shah I was assassinated shortly after Nizam al-Mulk , Taj al-Mulk nominated Mahmud as Sultan and set out for Isfahan ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d04", "start": 291, "end": 382, "text": "[ 2 ] Mahmud was a child , and his mother Terken Khatun wished to seize power in his name ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d04", "start": 383, "end": 498, "text": "To accomplish this , she entered in negotiations with her son-in-law , the Caliph al-Muqtadi , to secure her rule ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d04", "start": 499, "end": 522, "text": "The Caliph opposed both"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Mustafa II", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Osman III", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d01:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "Malik Shah I", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d02:c0", "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d03:c0", "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d04:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d00:c0", "entity": "Mahmud I's father", "scope": "explicitly stated", "claim": "Mahmud I's father was Mustafa II.", "answer": "Mustafa II", "quote": "He was born at Edirne Palace, the son of Mustafa II (1664–1703); his mother was Saliha Sabkati Valide Sultan.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0105-ae5224da23d8:d01:c0", "entity": "Mahmud I", "scop